{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"r8_hw","type":"text","text":"Kinect(v2) + Dancer + Designer\n↓\nLive gesture data → generative pattern + particles → procedural soundscape\n↓\n**Unreal Engine + TouchDesigner** → sound + image response","x":-1660,"y":4780,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"r8_prompt","type":"text","text":"## instructor's own practice\n\n---\n\n**Now: what would *your* cascade look like?**\n\nStart with your practice thinking.\nWork toward data.\nLet the sensor follow.\n\n→ [[../Documents/Hardware Clarifications — Thinking Toward Sensors|Thinking Toward Sensors]]","x":-840,"y":4780,"width":1100,"height":280,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"4816dcdd890b1fb9","type":"link","url":"https://www.darrenwoodlandjr.com/?pgid=m7trkt3a-f47806de-2398-45e1-a3f4-d65148a5ca70","x":-723,"y":5140,"width":866,"height":613},
		{"id":"r8_think","type":"text","text":"### Darren Woodland Jr. (That’s Me!)\n*Echoes of Harmonic Threads*\n\nBlack bodies and narratives driven by continually perpetuated historical traumas as expressed the the entanglements of sound, dance, and Afrofuturistic narrative.","x":-3300,"y":4780,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"r8_data","type":"text","text":"**Movement + Afrofuturism** → purpose built hydrophones as musical ←→ cultural ←→ scientific instruments\n\nThe Kinect (v2) abstracts movement into gesturally recognized skeletal figures that provide points of data along the landmarks of the body.","x":-2480,"y":4780,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"r7_think","type":"text","text":"### Rafael Lozano-Hemmer\n*Pulse Room (2006)*\n\nEvery visitor who has been here is still present — their heartbeat still in the room. What would it mean to make *presence accumulate* rather than vanish?","x":-3300,"y":4060,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"r7_data","type":"text","text":"**The body at rest** → pulse / heart rate → continuous biometric stream\n\nThe most intimate involuntary signal: a heartbeat. Data the body produces *without thinking*. Completely individual, completely universal.","x":-2480,"y":4060,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"r6_think","type":"text","text":"### David Rokeby\n*Very Nervous System (1982–1991)*\n\nWhat if the body could play an instrument not by touching it, but by moving through space? What *is* the instrument, if the instrument is the air itself?","x":-3300,"y":3440,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"r6_data","type":"text","text":"**Presence + movement** → optical flow from video\n\nThe camera reads motion vectors — not what the body looks like, but *how it is moving*. Velocity and direction become the raw material.","x":-2480,"y":3440,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"r7_hw","type":"text","text":"Pulse oximeter sensors (visitors hold a handle)\n↓\nCustom real-time system\n↓\n300 incandescent bulbs — each pulsing at the rhythm of a past visitor. Newest arrival displaces the oldest heartbeat.","x":-1660,"y":4060,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"r7_work","type":"link","url":"https://www.lozano-hemmer.com/pulse_room.php","x":-840,"y":4140,"width":1100,"height":480,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"r6_hw","type":"text","text":"Video camera + frame grabber (built 1982 — before Max/MSP existed)\n↓\nCustom C software → synthesizer control signals\n↓\nMovement generates sound in real time — no touch, no controller, no stage equipment","x":-1660,"y":3440,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"r6_work","type":"link","url":"https://vimeo.com/8120954","x":-840,"y":3440,"width":1100,"height":480,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"22d0e0fac8bcfdd5","type":"text","text":"https://vimeo.com/8120954?fl=pl&fe=cm","x":-368,"y":3920,"width":628,"height":50,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"0489d388d48b9636","type":"text","text":"https://www.lozano-hemmer.com/pulse_room.php","x":-460,"y":4620,"width":720,"height":60,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"r5_hw","type":"text","text":"Custom gloves (flex sensors, IMUs, WiFi module)\n↓\n**Max/MSP** + custom gesture mapping software\n↓\nReal-time synthesis, effects, looping, and arrangement — the hands become the studio","x":-1660,"y":2720,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"r5_work","type":"link","url":"https://mimugloves.com","x":-840,"y":2720,"width":1080,"height":480,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"2277945eb295c328","type":"text","text":"https://mimugloves.com","x":0,"y":3200,"width":240,"height":60,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"r5_think","type":"text","text":"### Imogen Heap\n*Mi.Mu Gloves*\n\nPerformance should be fully embodied. Why do singers stand static at a mic while all the sonic shaping happens offstage, invisible? The gesture should *be* the instrument.","x":-3300,"y":2720,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"r5_data","type":"text","text":"**Hand + finger position, orientation, gesture** → flex sensor readings + accelerometer/gyroscope data\n\nA vocabulary of gesture mapped to a vocabulary of sound. Moving a wrist is composing.","x":-2480,"y":2720,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"r4_think","type":"text","text":"### George Lewis\n*Voyager (1987–)*\n\nWhat would it mean for a machine to improvise in a Black musical tradition. Not mimicking it, but *thinking with it*? Can software carry cultural memory and agency?","x":-3300,"y":1960,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"r4_data","type":"text","text":"**Live instrumental performance** → MIDI: note, velocity, timing, pitch, density data\n\nThe data is *musical behavior* — not just notes but phrasing, energy, direction, momentum. The machine listens to all of it.","x":-2480,"y":1960,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"r4_hw","type":"text","text":"Any MIDI instrument (trombone, saxophone, piano)\n↓\n**Voyager** — custom Lisp-based AI improvisation system (built at STEIM, Amsterdam)\n↓\nVirtual improvising orchestra: responds to the player AND generates independently","x":-1660,"y":1960,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"r4_work","type":"link","url":"https://archiv.hkw.de/en/programm/projekte/2020/das_verschwinden_der_musik/programm_verschwinden_der_musik/video_george_lewis_timelike_weave_voyager.php","x":-840,"y":1960,"width":1080,"height":480,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"15c2ba45508583ad","type":"text","text":"https://archiv.hkw.de/en/programm/projekte/2020/das_verschwinden_der_musik/programm_verschwinden_der_musik/video_george_lewis_timelike_weave_voyager.php","x":-492,"y":2440,"width":732,"height":67,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"h_hw","type":"text","text":"**HARDWARE → SOFTWARE**\n*What transduces and processes?*","x":-1658,"y":-720,"width":700,"height":80,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"h_work","type":"text","text":"**THE WORK**\n*What becomes possible?*","x":-838,"y":-720,"width":740,"height":80,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"h_thinking","type":"text","text":"**PRACTICE THINKING**\n*What is the work obsessed with?*","x":-3298,"y":-720,"width":700,"height":80,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"h_data","type":"text","text":"**PHENOMENA + DATA**\n*What does the practice want to sense?*","x":-2478,"y":-720,"width":700,"height":80,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"cascade_title","type":"text","text":"# The Research-Creation Cascade\n## What Becomes Possible When Practice Leads\n\nEach row traces one practice's path: from curiosity → phenomena → hardware → software → work.\n\nThe cascade is not a pipeline. It is a question: *what does my practice want to know about the world, and what can transduce that?*","x":-2368,"y":-1760,"width":1400,"height":240,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"r1_hw","type":"text","text":"IR camera arrays + motion sensors\n↓\n**Isadora** — software they built themselves\n↓\nReal-time video, sound, and environment that respond to and shape the dancer","x":-1658,"y":-320,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"r1_work","type":"link","url":"https://troikaranch.org","x":-838,"y":-320,"width":1080,"height":480,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"r1_think","type":"text","text":"### Troika Ranch\n*Mark Coniglio + Dawn Stoppiello*\n\nWhat does it mean for a dancer's body to *generate* the world the performance inhabits? Can the performer simultaneously cause and be caused by the environment?","x":-3298,"y":-320,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"r1_data","type":"text","text":"**Movement** → body position, velocity, gesture in space\n\nInfrared camera tracking → continuous positional + gestural data streams in real time","x":-2478,"y":-320,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"r2_hw","type":"text","text":"Camera + motion capture\n↓\nCustom visualization software (OSU ACCAD + The Forsythe Company)\n↓\n89 interactive data objects — animations, scores, tools built from movement","x":-1658,"y":480,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"r2_work","type":"link","url":"https://synchronousobjects.osu.edu","x":-838,"y":480,"width":1080,"height":480,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"r2_think","type":"text","text":"### William Forsythe\n*Synchronous Objects for One Flat Thing, reproduced*\n\nChoreographic thinking doesn't disappear when the dance ends. Can movement organize things other than bodies? What other forms can choreographic structure take?","x":-3298,"y":480,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"r2_data","type":"text","text":"**Dance performance** → motion tracking → relational + structural data\n\nCuing patterns, spatial alignments, timing relationships extracted from a recorded piece of choreography","x":-2478,"y":480,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"34778f3dd6f4114c","type":"text","text":"https://synchronousobjects.osu.edu","x":-114,"y":960,"width":356,"height":53,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"7a2cab7d9f5f31e5","type":"text","text":"https://www.darrenwoodlandjr.com/?pgid=m7trkt3a-f47806de-2398-45e1-a3f4-d65148a5ca70","x":-149,"y":5012,"width":409,"height":97,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"64066ac92feaf8db","type":"text","text":"https://troikaranch.org","x":-8,"y":160,"width":250,"height":50,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"r3_hw","type":"text","text":"DIY handheld controllers + breath mouthpiece sensor + smartphone\n↓\n**Pure Data** + custom OSC routing\n↓\nFull live looping, synthesis, and arrangement — performed anywhere, no infrastructure needed","x":-1668,"y":1200,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"r3_work","type":"link","url":"https://www.ted.com/talks/onyx_ashanti_this_is_beatjazz","x":-848,"y":1200,"width":1080,"height":480,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"28fcfdbc507b4d91","type":"text","text":"https://www.ted.com/talks/onyx_ashanti_this_is_beatjazz","x":-300,"y":1680,"width":532,"height":50,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"r3_think","type":"text","text":"### Onyx Ashanti\n*beatjazz*\n\nThe Black body as a fully sovereign instrument. Full-spectrum musical autonomy — composition, performance, improvisation — all *in and from the body*. No stage, no studio, no separation between thinking and sounding.","x":-3308,"y":1200,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"r3_data","type":"text","text":"**Hand position + breath + full-body movement** → continuous gesture + breath data\n\nThe body IS the instrument and the interface — not a metaphor but literally. Every movement is a performance decision.","x":-2488,"y":1200,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"r10_work","type":"link","url":"https://www.memo.tv/works/learning-to-see/","x":-840,"y":6800,"width":1080,"height":480,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"r10_data","type":"text","text":"**Live video** → real-time pixel data from a webcam\n\nBut the data the model *actually uses* is its training set — tens of thousands of images of natural phenomena. The webcam is the trigger. The dataset is the lens.","x":-2480,"y":6800,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"r10_hw","type":"text","text":"Webcam → GPU compute\n↓\nCustom deep learning — trained *only* on natural phenomena (ocean, fire, clouds, aurora)\n↓\nLive video of hands and objects rendered in real time as whatever the model was trained to recognize","x":-1660,"y":6800,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"r10_think","type":"text","text":"### Memo Akten\n*Learning to See (2017–)*\n\nA neural network can only see through the filter of what it has already seen. What does that tell us about *all* seeing — human or machine? Perception is never a window. It's always a worldview.","x":-3300,"y":6800,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"r9_work","type":"link","url":"https://www.blasttheory.co.uk/projects/can-you-see-me-now/","x":-840,"y":6000,"width":1080,"height":480,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"r9_think","type":"text","text":"### Blast Theory\n*Can You See Me Now? (2001)*\n\nUrban space as game board. Being seen, or not, as the actual stakes. What happens when players on the internet and runners in a physical city occupy and threaten each other in the *same* space?","x":-3300,"y":6000,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"r9_data","type":"text","text":"**Physical location + network presence** → GPS coordinates, player proximity, connection status\n\nBeing caught = your GPS position and a runner's GPS position intersect. Presence is literally data. Absence is too.","x":-2480,"y":6000,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"r9_hw","type":"text","text":"GPS receivers (worn by street runners) + handheld computers + walkie-talkies + networked server\n↓\nCustom real-time game engine + live mapping (Mixed Reality Lab, Nottingham)\n↓\nMixed-reality chase: online players as avatars; runners as live GPS dots in the city","x":-1660,"y":6000,"width":700,"height":280,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"bea8029656ef02f4","x":-310,"y":6480,"width":550,"height":50,"color":"2","type":"text","text":"https://www.blasttheory.co.uk/projects/can-you-see-me-now/"},
		{"id":"9369edb7d04ccacf","x":-180,"y":7280,"width":420,"height":67,"color":"5","type":"text","text":"https://www.memo.tv/works/learning-to-see/"},
		{"id":"legend","type":"text","text":"**🟠 Movement / Dance / Interactive**\n**🟣 Afrofuturist / Black Practice**\n**🟡 Sound / Music**\n**🔵 Computer Vision / ML-Visual**\n**🟢 Biometric / Body**\n**🔴 Instructor Practice**","x":-1808,"y":-1280,"width":280,"height":220,"color":"1"}
	],
